Silo patch 0001 — let the caller choose where the named loader link goes
=======================================================================

WHAT UPSTREAM ALREADY DOES (all of this is CrossOver FOSS, dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c,
marked "CW HACK 22144 ... which will show up as the icon name in the Dock"):
  * create_tempdir()                  -> $TMPDIR/winetemp-<ino>-<size>-<mtime_s>-<mtime_ns>/
                                         mkdir it, and symlink ntdll.so into it
  * create_preloader_link()           -> hard link the loader into that dir under the exe's name
  * replace_wineloader_path_with_link -> exec THAT path, so the process is named after the exe
  * gated on `if (getenv("WINEDLLPATH"))`

WHY WE PATCH IT
  On macOS 27 the Dock still honours the icon winemac.drv sets at runtime
  (setApplicationIconImage), but Mission Control and Stage Manager read the icon of the
  process's *bundle* — and a Wine process has none, so they draw the generic "exec" icon.
  Measured on device; CrossOver's own steam.exe measures identical (bundleIdentifier = nil,
  generic icon) and only looks right because a separate bundled app owns its window, via the
  --enable-alt-loader machinery that is NOT part of the FOSS source drop.
  The fix needs the exec'd path to be inside a real .app. Upstream already puts the loader link
  in a directory of its choosing and already solves the hard part (the ntdll.so symlink, which
  init_paths() realpath()s to recover the runtime's true dll_dir/bin_dir/data_dir). So all we
  need is to let the caller pick that directory.

WHAT THIS PATCH ADDS
  SILO_LOADER_LINK_DIR — when set and non-empty, used verbatim as the link directory, and the
  mechanism fires on it as well as on WINEDLLPATH. Silo points it at a per-game
  <Name>.app/Contents/MacOS. Measured (without Wine, on plain GUI binaries): an executable inside
  a bundle reports that bundle's identity, icon and CFBundleName even when its filename does NOT
  match CFBundleExecutable — so ONE bundle per game covers every Wine process it spawns
  (the game exe, explorer.exe, steamwebhelper.exe ...).

SAFETY
  Unset (the default, and every non-Silo build) = byte-identical upstream behaviour. If the
  directory is missing or unwritable, link()/symlink() fail, create_preloader_link() returns NULL
  and the loader path is left untouched — it degrades to upstream, it does not fail the launch.
  We deliberately do NOT set WINEDLLPATH: that would change module search on the GPTK/DXMT
  critical path (LaunchOrchestrator.makePlan documents "no WINEDLLPATH").

NOTE ON STYLE
  The moved block inside the new `else` is left at its original indentation on purpose, to keep
  this diff as small as possible — it has to be re-applied to every new CrossOver source release.

NOT YET VERIFIED ON DEVICE: needs a Wine build (this box has Command Line Tools only, so CI).
The open question is whether the renamed loader finds ntdll.so with no WINEDLLPATH set; if it
does not, the one-line follow-up is to setenv WINEDLLPATH from dll_dir inside create_tempdir.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c	2026-09-19 14:15:39
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c	2026-09-19 14:15:39
@@ -565,13 +565,37 @@
 /* Returns a path to $TMPDIR/winetemp-<wineloader_inode>-<wineloader_size_in_bytes>-<wineloader_mtime_sec>-<-wineloader_mtime_nsec>
  * The intention is that all links to the same wineloader will go in the same directory, and a different directory
  * will be used if wineloader is updated or modified.
+ *
+ * SILO PATCH: when SILO_LOADER_LINK_DIR is set and non-empty, that directory is used verbatim
+ * instead of the $TMPDIR one. Silo points it at a per-game <Name>.app/Contents/MacOS, so the link
+ * this function is about to be given is exec'd from inside a real application bundle and macOS
+ * attributes the window to it — which is what makes the icon and the name correct in the Dock AND
+ * in Mission Control / Stage Manager (measured on macOS 27: those two surfaces read the bundle
+ * icon and ignore the one winemac.drv sets at runtime via setApplicationIconImage).
+ * The ntdll.so symlink created below is what keeps this correct wherever the directory is: the
+ * loader finds ntdll.so as "<its own dir>/ntdll.so", and init_paths() then realpath()s that
+ * symlink to recover the true dll_dir / bin_dir / data_dir of the runtime.
+ * Unset (the default) means byte-identical upstream behaviour.
  */
 static char *create_tempdir(const char *wineloader_path)
 {
     char *str, *ntdll, *p, *tempdir = malloc(MAX_PATH);
+    const char *link_dir = getenv("SILO_LOADER_LINK_DIR");
     struct stat st;
     size_t n;
 
+    if (link_dir && *link_dir)
+    {
+        if (strlcpy(tempdir, link_dir, MAX_PATH) >= MAX_PATH)
+            goto fail;
+
+        /* the code below appends the exe name straight onto this, so keep a trailing slash */
+        n = strlen(tempdir);
+        if (n && tempdir[n - 1] != '/' && strlcat(tempdir, "/", MAX_PATH) >= MAX_PATH)
+            goto fail;
+    }
+    else
+    {
     if (!confstr(_CS_DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR, tempdir, MAX_PATH))
         goto fail;
 
@@ -585,6 +609,7 @@
     free(str);
     if (n >= MAX_PATH)
         goto fail;
+    }
 
     /* mkdir may fail if the directory already exists but that's ok */
     mkdir(tempdir, 0700);
@@ -678,8 +703,16 @@
      * which will show up as the icon name in the Dock.
      * When the preloader is not being used, WINEDLLPATH needs to be set correctly for
      * the loader to find ntdll.so, so don't even attempt this unless WINEDLLPATH is set.
+     *
+     * SILO PATCH: also fire when SILO_LOADER_LINK_DIR is set. The WINEDLLPATH precondition
+     * above is about finding ntdll.so, and create_tempdir() puts an ntdll.so symlink right
+     * next to the link it makes, which is one of the paths the loader searches. Silo therefore
+     * does NOT have to set WINEDLLPATH — deliberately, because that would change module search
+     * on the GPTK/DXMT-critical path (see LaunchOrchestrator.makePlan, "no WINEDLLPATH").
+     * If the link cannot be made, create_preloader_link() returns NULL and the loader path is
+     * left untouched, so a missing/unwritable directory degrades to upstream behaviour.
      */
-    if (getenv("WINEDLLPATH"))
+    if (getenv("WINEDLLPATH") || getenv("SILO_LOADER_LINK_DIR"))
         replace_wineloader_path_with_link( &(argv[1]), image_path );
 #endif
 
